svga: change the screen's resource counters atomically.

hud.num_resources, hud.total_resource_bytes and hud.num_failed_allocations
belong to the screen, but every context of the screen creates and destroys
resources -- and a WebKit web process has several, on as many threads: the
main thread, the compositor and the Skia GPU workers, all sharing one
screen.  The counters were plain ++ and --, so two threads updating them at
once lose an update.  A lost increment leaves num_resources one short; when
the last resources are destroyed (a web process shutting down destroys its
GL contexts while a worker thread releases its Skia context) the count
reaches zero early and the next destroy fails

  svga_resource_destroy: Assertion `ss->hud.num_resources > 0' failed.

which aborts the process.

